      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/858c86/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-03-01T19:56:26.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I'm sure we played this right, but we had an interesting situation last session:</p><p>The Tachyon player wanted to play Supersonic Response on the first turn.&nbsp; The villain had damaged her previously.&nbsp; However, the card wording is \"If that target dealt Tachyon damage since your last turn, she deals that target 2 sonic damage.\"&nbsp; The problem is that even though the villain had damaged Tachyon, she hadn't had a turn yet, so the exact condition of the card wasn't met.</p><p>We played it by what we assume was the&nbsp;intent of the card and went ahead with the 2 sonic damage.&nbsp; What does everyone else think?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:40:37.937Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
